                A field of colorful wildflowers blankets the Atacama Desert in northern Chile, transforming the world&apos;s driest non-polar desert into a vibrant landscape during the rare flowering desert phenomenon, known locally as the Desierto Florido, or Desert Bloom.
                
                    
                    Tamara Merino for NPR
                    
                
                hide caption
            
        

            
              
